  "description": "AGLedger service overview: is it up, is it fast, is it moving records, and is anything saturated. The two sibling dashboards answer narrower questions (data integrity, silent drops); start here. Every panel resolves on a stock single-node install, and the worker-owned panels resolve because the bundled Prometheus scrapes both processes.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Total HTTP request rate across every route.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(agledger_http_request_duration_seconds_count[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Requests/sec",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Requests/sec",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Share of requests answered 5xx over the last 5 minutes. Reads 0% on a healthy install rather than \"No data\": the numerator carries `or vector(0)` because sum() over an empty vector is empty, not zero, and an empty numerator would make this blank exactly when there are no errors, indistinguishable from a misconfigured datasource.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(agledger_http_request_duration_seconds_count{status_code=~\"5..\"}[5m])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min(sum(rate(agledger_http_request_duration_seconds_count[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "Error rate (5xx)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Error rate (5xx)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
